cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this edition, please cite it as below and state that the Chinese translation, notes and
  scansion were generated by AI. Cite individual verses with their IDs, e.g. africa.9.123.
title: "Petrarch's Africa: Latin–Chinese parallel edition with notes, scansion and recitation script"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Claude (Anthropic)"
  - alias: yiyuanli939
repository-code: "https://github.com/yiyuanli939/Africa-by-Petrarca"
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-19"
keywords:
  - Petrarch
  - Petrarca
  - Africa
  - Latin
  - Chinese translation
  - dactylic hexameter
  - scansion
  - digital edition
  - TEI
  - text-to-speech
abstract: >-
  Francesco Petrarca's Latin epic Africa (9 books, 6,730 verses) with a line-by-line Chinese verse
  translation made directly from the Latin, 1,381 notes, a metrical scansion of every verse and an
  ElevenLabs recitation script. All material is line-addressed (JSONL, TSV, TEI P5). The translation,
  notes and scansion were produced and cross-reviewed by AI agents and have not yet been reviewed by
  a human Latinist.
